amendmentsChecked.detail:
setLayer returns early when the entry is not a layer or `layer.render === render`. request() returns false without recording when open equals the effective state, or equals the applied state. The spec 'an unchanged request records nothing and an unchanged layer emits nothing…' asserts:
- zero emits for an unchanged close and open;
- unchanged version and layersOf identity;
- setLayer(null) twice gives no emit;
- setLayer('body') twice gives exactly one emit.
Mutant M5 (emit on unchanged value) fails that spec. Mutant M6 (drop the first unchanged-request guard) survives, but it is near-equivalent: the second guard (`open === applied`) still records nothing, so the amendment (c) behaviour is intact.

frontend/libs/ui/README.md: the new paragraph sits between '### 6.12' (:175) and '### 6.13' (:193). It covers:
- one modal at a time, with layering;
- screens keep overlays as siblings, never nested or swapped by hand;
- no useLocalSearchParams or useRouter in an overlay body;
- 'A layer appears and leaves without motion';
- the RupeeInput pad is not a kit overlay and chains only from inside a presented Sheet or Dialog.
docs/15-decisions-log.md gains row E10, one line. docs/22 is untouched.

